{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-26T19:02:14.338Z","author":"harness:codex","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"9a3d0027739dfadbcc41b040","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"probe"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-gh1607"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-1607: Provide intent-specific recovery for unsupported block and unblock commands"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"**Version:** pm 2026.10.26.\n\n**Repro**\n```sh\npm block <id> --reason waiting\npm unblock <id> --note ready\n```\n**Observed:** both exit 2. `block` suggests `github blockers` and `list --status blocked` (read-only surfaces); `unblock` prints generic examples (`activity`, `aggregate`, `assurance`, …). Neither points at the supported local mutation.\n\n**Expected:** intent-specific recovery for these lifecycle verbs, e.g.\n```sh\npm update <id> --blocked-by <blocker> --blocked-reason \"waiting\"\npm update <id> --dep-remove <blocker> --unset blocked_by --unset blocked_reason --unblock-note \"ready\"\n```\nor first-class `block`/`unblock` aliases that map to those flags (never auto-executing a guessed mutation).\n\n**Why it matters for agents:** block/unblock are the verbs agents reach for during a work session; today the failed call is followed by a help search and another attempt (~600–750 bytes of unhelpful stderr each). Note that `--unblock-note` alone records a note but does not remove the blocker edge, which is easy to get wrong without a worked example.\n\n\nIntake boundary: this is a report against published 2026.10.26, not proof of a current-checkout defect. Reproduce in an external sandbox before implementation. Related completed work retains its shipped scope. Proposed examples or categories are not accepted contracts until validated.\n\nSource: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1607"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","github","sdk"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-10-26T19:02:14.338Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-26T19:02:14.338Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:codex"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":90},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Derive examples from live update contracts and prove the suggested block and unblock workflows on isolated trackers.; Unblock recovery explains removal of the actual blocker relationship and stale blocker metadata; a note alone is not presented as unblocking.; Refusals preserve the usage exit code, leave data unchanged, identify the intended lifecycle surface, and retain extension-command and ambiguity behavior. Any new alias must have a declared SDK/CLI/MCP contract."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-f05lsg"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"Unsupported lifecycle verbs lead to a correct local mutation recipe with explicit identifiers and blocker-edge cleanup, without automatically executing an inferred mutation."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-1p6f","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-10-26T19:02:14.338Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-in23qu","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-10-26T19:02:14.338Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:02:14.338Z","author":"harness:codex","text":"Duplicate check: fresh orientation, request-specific search, open/in-progress inventories and complete strict 3126-item all-status corpus found no open owner for this exact case. Full live metadata and histories of related owners confirm their completed, distinct scope. This is intake only, open and unclaimed; implementation is outside the current delivery cohort."}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/escape_class","value":"production_defect"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"2dae3d235635fab349cae8fe0069c744ad183d693e7e22dcd41cd29f28bf524d","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"a8fc603314e3835f17bd15f9cfdf81b7f23edf863fba836a14113a9f085bdef9"}
